---
import NoticeLayout from "@/layouts/NoticeLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@/site.config";
---

<NoticeLayout title="Privacy notice" description="How visiting this website and contacting its operator involve personal data.">
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name}, based in {site.location}, is responsible for personal data
    processed in connection with operating this website and handling enquiries.
    For privacy questions or requests, email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    This notice describes the current website and contact arrangements, with
    reference to the Swiss Federal Act on Data Protection and other data
    protection laws where applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The website has no visitor accounts, contact forms, advertising or analytics scripts.</li>
    <li>The site's own code does not set cookies or use browser storage to track visitors.</li>
    <li>GitHub Pages hosts the site and processes technical data when you visit.</li>
    <li>Your browser requests fonts from Google when a page loads.</li>
    <li>Using an email link opens your email application; it does not submit a form on this website.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting and technical data</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Requests
    to load pages and files disclose technical information to the hosting service,
    including your IP address. GitHub states that it logs and stores visitors'
    IP addresses for security purposes, even when visitors are not signed in.
    Hosting data is used to deliver and protect the service. GitHub controls
    retention of its hosting logs; this website does not set a separate retention
    period for those logs. See
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">GitHub Pages data collection</a>
    and the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    The site loads the Inter and Fraunces typefaces from Google's servers at
    fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com. Your browser connects to Google
    to request the font styles and files, disclosing your IP address and request
    information such as browser headers. These requests enable the site's
    typography. You can block these domains using browser settings or a content
    blocker; the site will use fallback fonts. See
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Email correspondence</h2>
  <p>
    If you email {site.email}, your address, message and any details you provide
    are processed to respond to your enquiry and manage any resulting professional
    correspondence. Messages are handled through Gmail, provided by Google,
    and through the email providers involved in delivery. Please only include
    information needed for your enquiry and avoid sending sensitive personal or
    patient data by ordinary email.
  </p>
  <!-- Owner review: confirm the email-handling and retention practice below before publication. -->
  <p>
    Correspondence is kept for as long as needed to handle the enquiry and any
    follow-up, or to meet applicable record-keeping obligations, then deleted
    when it is no longer needed. Where a message becomes part of a research or
    contractual relationship, additional retention requirements may apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers and international processing</h2>
  <p>
    GitHub and Google receive data as described above. Their services involve
    processing in the United States and other countries outside Switzerland.
    Their privacy notices explain their processing locations, safeguards and
    arrangements for international data transfers. These providers also have
    responsibilities for processing they carry out for their own purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Links to publications, professional profiles and other websites, including
    RIDA, take you to separately operated services. The social profile links are
    ordinary links, rather than embedded social widgets. When you follow a link,
    the destination receives technical information about your visit and applies
    its own privacy practices. Consult its privacy notice before providing data.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    Subject to applicable law, you can request access to personal data held about
    you, correction of inaccurate data, or deletion, and object to processing.
    Other rights, including data portability, may apply depending on the
    circumstances. Send requests to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    Identity verification may be needed to protect your information. Requests
    about data held independently by GitHub or Google can also be directed to
    those providers using their privacy contact channels.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can raise a data protection concern with the
    <a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/en">Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)</a>
    or another competent supervisory authority where applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice will be revised when the website's services or data processing
    change. The date above indicates the latest revision.
  </p>
</NoticeLayout>
